  "body": "## Finding description \n\nThe rewards distribution mechanism suffers a critical precision loss issue, \nwhen distributing reward amounts to a large number of shareholders,  \ncausing complete loss of funds due to truncation in the `getAccRewardsPerShare` calculation.\n\nRoot Cause\n\nThe `getAccRewardsPerShare` function [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/main/contracts/launchpad/libraries/RewardsTracker.sol#L209-L228) in `RewardsTracker.sol` uses integer division that truncates to zero when `(pendingRewards * PRECISION_FACTOR) < totalShares` , \npermanently losing reward amounts.\n\n```solidity\n    function getAccRewardsPerShare(RewardPoolData storage self)\n        internal view\n        returns (uint256 accBaseRewardsPerShare, uint256 accQuoteRewardsPerShare)\n    {\n        uint96 totalShares = self.totalShares;\n        if (totalShares == 0) return (self.accBaseRewardPerShare, self.accQuoteRewardPerShare);\n\n        accBaseRewardsPerShare = self.accBaseRewardPerShare;\n        accQuoteRewardsPerShare = self.accQuoteRewardPerShare;\n\n        if (self.pendingBaseRewards > 0) {\n            accBaseRewardsPerShare += ((self.pendingBaseRewards * PRECISION_FACTOR) / uint128(totalShares));\n        }\n\n        if (self.pendingQuoteRewards > 0) {\n            accQuoteRewardsPerShare += ((self.pendingQuoteRewards * PRECISION_FACTOR) / uint128(totalShares));\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nNote : total shares can be upto 800 Million (8e26) in a fully sold out bonding curve. \n\n\nProvided the distributor contract has a non-zero `pendingBaseRewards` or `pendingQuoteRewards` ,\nThe `getAccRewardsPerShare` function is triggered thru `update` every time an user claims or transfers their launchTokens purchased from bonding curves.\n\nMeanwhile, the `GTELaunchpadV2Pair` contract continuously adds small reward amounts to the distributor in the form of swap fees. \n\nUnder this scenario,  \nall these rewards are permanently lost due to the truncation issue as described in below examples.\n\nExample A: USDC (6 decimals) Quote Token\n```solidity\n// Scenario: 400M total shares, 1000 USDC reward added\ntotalShares = 400,000,000 * 1e18 = 4e26\npendingQuoteRewards = 1000 * 1e6\n\n// Calculation:\naccQuoteRewardsPerShare += (1e9 * 1e12) / 4e26\n                        += 1e21 / 4e26 \n                        += 0 (truncated) \n\n// Result: 1000 USDC permanently lost\n// Minimum reward needed: 4e26 / 1e12 = 4e14 = 400,000,000 USDC\n```\n\nExample B: WETH (18 decimals) Quote Token\n```solidity\n// Scenario: 400M total shares, 0.001 WETH reward from swap fees  \ntotalShares = 400,000,000 * 1e18 = 4e26\npendingQuoteRewards = 0.001 * 1e18 = 1e15\n\n// Calculation:\naccQuoteRewardsPerShare += (1e15 * 1e12) / 4e26\n                        += 1e27 / 4e26 = 10/4\n                        += 2 (truncation) (should be 2.5)\n\n// User with 1M shares gets: (1e24 * 2) / 1e12 = 2e12 wei = 0.000002 ETH\n// But total distributed: (4e26 * 2) / 1e12 = 8e14 = 0.0008 ETH\n\noriginalReward = 0.001 ETH\nactualDistributed = 0.0008 ETH  \n\n// Loss: 0.001 - 0.0008 = 0.0002 ETH (20% precision loss)\n```\n\n## Impact and Likelihood\n\n1. Permanent loss of funds - Truncated rewards are not recoverable.\n2. All swap fees distributed thru the pair contract are lost, \n   creating significant cumulative losses over time\n3. Fee share holders lose earned rewards from AMM trading activity.\n4. Unusable reward mechanism \n5. Affects every launchToken graduated thru bonding curve\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSeveral ways to fix \n\nMethod 1 : Use a higher precision factor\n\nMethod 2: Reward accumulation threshold\n\n```solidity\nuint256 public constant MIN_REWARD_THRESHOLD = totalShares / PRECISION_FACTOR;\n\nif (pendingRewards < MIN_REWARD_THRESHOLD) {\n    // Accumulate in separate storage until threshold met\n    accumulatedSmallRewards += pendingRewards;\n    return;\n}\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "A runnable PoC to be used in the `PoCLaunchpad.t` contract \nDemonstrates substantial loss of rewards due to precision loss.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {LaunchpadTestBase} from \"./LaunchpadTestBase.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\n\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\n\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is  LaunchpadTestBase  {\n    /**\n     * PoC can utilize the following variables to access the relevant contracts:\n     * - factory: ERC1967Factory.sol \n     * - launchpad: Launchpad.sol\n     * - distributor: Distributor.sol\n     * - curve: SimpleBondingCurve.sol\n     * - launchpadLPVault: LaunchpadLPVault.sol\n     * - quoteToken: Quote token used in Launchpad system\n     * - uniV2Router: Uniswap V2 Router used in Launchpad system\n     */\n // forge test --match-path test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol --match-test test_divisionTruncationRewardLoss -vvv\nfunction test_divisionTruncationRewardLoss() external {\n\n        LaunchToken launchToken = LaunchToken(token);\n        \n        // Create test users\n        address alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n        address bob = makeAddr(\"bob\");\n        address dave = makeAddr(\"dave\");\n        \n        console.log(\"Alice:\", alice);\n        console.log(\"Bob:\", bob);\n        console.log(\"Dave:\", dave);\n        \n        // Step 1: Setup bonding phase purchases\n        _setupBondingPurchases(launchToken, alice, bob);\n        \n        // Step 2: Graduate the token\n        _graduateToken(launchToken, dave);\n        \n        // Step 3: Demonstrate the vulnerability\n        _demonstrateVulnerability(launchToken, alice, dave);\n    }\n    \n    function _setupBondingPurchases(LaunchToken launchToken, address alice, address bob) internal {\n        // Alice buys 10 tokens during bonding phase\n        uint256 aliceAmount = 10e18;\n        uint256 aliceQuote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, aliceAmount, true);\n        \n        quoteToken.mint(alice, aliceQuote);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), aliceQuote);\n        \n        vm.prank(alice);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: alice,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: alice,\n                amountOutBase: aliceAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: aliceQuote\n            })\n        );\n\n        // Bob buys 20 tokens during bonding phase\n        uint256 bobAmount = 20e18;\n        uint256 bobQuote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, bobAmount, true);\n        \n        quoteToken.mint(bob, bobQuote);\n        vm.prank(bob);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), bobQuote);\n        \n        vm.prank(bob);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: bob,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: bob,\n                amountOutBase: bobAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: bobQuote\n            })\n        );\n\n    }\n    \n    function _graduateToken(LaunchToken launchToken, address dave) internal {\n        // Dave buys remaining tokens to graduate the pair\n        uint256 bondingSupply = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        uint256 soldSoFar = curve.baseSoldFromCurve(token);\n        uint256 remainingAmount = bondingSupply - soldSoFar;\n        uint256 daveQuote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, remainingAmount, true);\n        \n        quoteToken.mint(dave, daveQuote);\n        vm.prank(dave);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), daveQuote);\n        \n        vm.prank(dave);\n        launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: dave,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: dave,\n                amountOutBase: remainingAmount,\n                maxAmountInQuote: daveQuote\n            })\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n=== After Dave graduates the token ===\");\n        console.log(\"Token unlocked (graduated):\", launchToken.unlocked());\n        console.log(\"Dave balance:\", launchToken.balanceOf(dave));\n        console.log(\"Dave bonding share:\", launchToken.bondingShare(dave));\n        console.log(\"Total fee share:\", launchToken.totalFeeShare());\n    }\n\n\n    function _demonstrateVulnerability(LaunchToken launchToken, address alice, address dave) internal {\n        console.log(\"\\n=== CRITICAL: Division Truncation in Real Contract Functions ===\");\n        \n        // Get current state after graduation\n        // Total shares can be as high as 800M (realistic high participation scenario)\n        uint256 totalShares = launchToken.totalFeeShare();  \n        console.log(\"Total fee shares after graduation:\", totalShares, \"800M (8e26)\" );\n        console.log(\"Alice bonding share:\", launchToken.bondingShare(alice));\n        console.log(\"Dave bonding share:\", launchToken.bondingShare(dave));\n\n        \n        // Constants from RewardsTracker\n        uint256 PRECISION_FACTOR = 1e12;\n    \n        console.log(\"\\n=== Scenario 2: Large USDC Reward (1000 USDC) ===\");\n        uint256 largeReward = 1000e6; // 1000 USDC\n        \n        // Demonstrate truncation even with large rewards when shares are high\n        console.log(\"Large reward amount:\", largeReward, \"wei (1000 USDC)\");\n        console.log(\"With 800M shares, let's see the truncation:\");\n        \n        // Total shares can be as high as 800M (realistic high participation scenario)\n        uint256 largeRewardPerShare = (largeReward * PRECISION_FACTOR) / totalShares;\n        uint256 actualDistributed = (largeRewardPerShare * totalShares) / PRECISION_FACTOR;\n        uint256 lostAmount = largeReward - actualDistributed;\n        \n        console.log(\"Simulated 800M total shares:\", totalShares);\n        console.log(\"Reward per share:\", largeRewardPerShare);\n        console.log(\"Actually distributed:\", actualDistributed, \"wei\");\n        console.log(\"Lost to truncation:\", lostAmount, \"wei\");\n        console.log(\"Percentage lost:\", (lostAmount * 100) / largeReward, \"%\");\n        \n        // Add the large reward to actual contract\n        quoteToken.mint(address(this), largeReward);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(distributor), largeReward);\n        \n        (, uint256 daveQuoteBefore2) = Distributor(distributor).getPendingRewards(token, dave);\n        IDistributor(distributor).addRewards(token, address(quoteToken), 0, uint128(largeReward));\n\n        \n        // CRITICAL: update() is only triggered during increaseStake/decreaseStake\n        // Trigger update() by having Dave transfer tokens to Alice (triggers decreaseStake)\n        vm.prank(dave);\n        launchToken.transfer(alice, 1e18); // Dave transfers 1 token to Alice\n        console.log(\"Dave transferred 1 token to Alice - this triggers update() and division truncation!\");\n\n        (, uint256 daveQuoteAfter2) = Distributor(distributor).getPendingRewards(token, dave);\n        \n        uint256 daveActualIncrease = daveQuoteAfter2 - daveQuoteBefore2;\n        console.log(\"Dave's actual reward increase:\", daveActualIncrease, \"wei\");\n        \n        // Calculate Alice's expected share\n        uint256 daveExpectedShare = (largeReward * launchToken.bondingShare(dave)) / totalShares;\n        console.log(\"Dave's expected share:\", daveExpectedShare, \"USDC in wei\");\n        console.log(\"Dave's actual loss:\", (daveExpectedShare - daveActualIncrease) , \"USDC in wei\");\n        \n        console.log(\"\\n=== CRITICAL VULNERABILITY SUMMARY ===\");\n        console.log(\"Even at a conservative 100M shares, substantial rewards get truncated\");\n        \n        console.log(\"\\nSEVERITY: CRITICAL - Loss of funds via division truncation\");\n\n        assertTrue(lostAmount > 0, \"Even Large rewards suffer truncation\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n```",
